# Clean Architecture

## Dependências (sempre para dentro)

| Camada | Importa | Proibido |
|--------|---------|----------|
| `packages/domain` | — | application, infrastructure, apps, fastify, drizzle, bullmq |
| `packages/application` | domain | infrastructure, ORM, HTTP clients |
| `packages/infrastructure` | domain (+ application raro) | apps |
| `apps/api`, `apps/worker` | application, infrastructure | Drizzle/schema direto em controllers |

## Onde colocar código novo

- Entidades, VOs (`Price`, `Slug`), eventos, interfaces → `packages/domain` (English names)
- Use cases (`GetProductBySlug`, `UpdatePricesBatch`) → `packages/application`
- Drizzle repos, Redis, BullMQ, fetchers Amazon/Shopee, email → `packages/infrastructure`
- Controllers, Zod schemas request, presenters → `apps/api/adapters`
- Processors, schedulers, event handlers → `apps/worker`
- DI/composition root → `packages/infrastructure/di/` (único lugar com classes concretas)

## Padrões obrigatórios

- **Repository:** interface em `domain/repositories`, implementação em `infrastructure/persistence`
- **Strategy + Factory:** `IMarketplaceFetcher` por marketplace; resolver via `MarketplaceFetcherFactory`
- **Domain Events:** `PriceDropped` publicado por use case; email via fila `domain_events` → handler separado
- **Mapper/Presenter:** DB row ↔ Entity ↔ ResponseDTO — entidade não conhece JSON HTTP

## Anti-patterns

```typescript
// ❌ SQL ou Redis no controller/use case
// ❌ import drizzle from 'apps/api/...'
// ❌ nodemailer.sendMail dentro de UpdatePricesBatch
// ✅ await this.eventBus.publish(new PriceDropped(...))
```

Substituir ORM/fila/email = reimplementar `infrastructure/` apenas; domain/application intactos.
